  route)
    # contract route "<plan>" --try <spec> [--try <spec> ...] [--parent <pid>]
    #
    # Backend-selection IS a /contract, not an agent decision baked into an
    # action. This verb constructs a funnel-first organ where each --try
    # spec becomes a real child cell with its own pointer-type (machine:,
    # sandbox:, runpod:, tool-guard:, …). Children are iterated in declared
    # order until ONE PASSes (first-available wins, OR-gate semantics). The
    # full routing graph is visible in `contract status <organ>` — no hidden
    # logic, no agent guessing which backend; the substrate composes.
    #
    # Origin: contract `386497eb` plank 2 (layer-router auto-pick). Realised
