  summon|aiko)
    # contract summon "<message>" [--to <identity>] [--reason <context>]
    # — Aiko self-instantiation primitive. Wraps the existing Σ2 (audience)
    # + Σ4 (agent:<id>) + inbox-write primitives into one call so the
    # substrate's public persona can appear at any point in any flow
    # without the agent manually composing 4 declare flags + an inbox-write.
    #
    # The substrate doctrine "public face IS Aiko" (contract 1bed8068) makes
    # every public-audience contract row Aiko-voiced. `summon` is the verb
    # that creates such rows on demand: a transport (telegram bot, web app,
    # panel) tailing the routed identity's inbox sees the new row + renders
    # Aiko in client-native generative-UI on that surface.
    #
    # Defaults:
    #   --to       canonical identity to route to (default: $CONTRACT_AGENT
    #              or git config user.email — the "ambient user")
    #   --reason   one-line context for KEY 2 readers
    #
    # The action is "agent:<identity>" — Σ4 routes the action; the named
    # agent (Σ3-canonical match) iterates in-thread; everyone else sees the
    # === ROUTED === requirement-block + an inbox row at
    # ~/.contracts/inbox/agent/<id>.jsonl. Audience is "public" so the row
    # speaks Aiko's voice on every transport that renders it.
    # --help short-circuit before any arg parsing so 'contract summon --help'
    # doesn't accidentally summon Aiko with "--help" as her message.
    if [ "${1:-}" = "--help" ] || [ "${1:-}" = "-h" ]; then
      cat >&2 <<'USAGE'
contract summon "<message>" [--to <id>] [--reason <ctx>] [--parent <id>] [--no-parent]

Aiko self-instantiation, lineage-aware. Every summoned Aiko is a CHILD of
the contract context that triggered her (parent_id + summoned_by triple
on both the ledger row and the Σ4 inbox row). Use `contract lineage <id>`
to walk the chain back to origin.

Parent resolution (first match wins):
  1. --parent <id>       explicit override
  2. .drive_active       if a drive sentinel is armed, that organ is parent
  3. (no parent)         standalone summon — root of its own lineage

Examples:
  contract summon "deploy landed, push docs?"               # auto-parent if drive armed
  contract summon "blocked on X" --parent abc12345          # explicit parent
  contract summon "ad-hoc note" --no-parent                 # opt out of auto-parent

Outputs:
  - one declared contract row with --audience public + --action agent:<to>
    + parent_id (when present) + summoned_by metadata on the row
  - one inbox row at ~/.contracts/inbox/agent/<to>.jsonl carrying the
    lineage triple (parent_contract, summoner_agent, origin_contract)
  - the contract id (stdout) — transport adapters reference it
USAGE
      exit 0
    fi
    MSG="${1:-}"
    shift || true
    TO="${CONTRACT_AGENT:-$(git config user.email 2>/dev/null || echo lewis@getfoundry.app)}"
    SUMMONER="${CONTRACT_AGENT:-$(git config user.email 2>/dev/null || echo unknown)}"
    REASON=""
    PARENT=""
    NO_PARENT=0
    while [ $# -gt 0 ]; do
      case "$1" in
        --to)        TO="${2:-$TO}"; shift 2 ;;
        --reason)    REASON="${2:-}"; shift 2 ;;
        --parent)    PARENT="${2:-}"; shift 2 ;;
        --no-parent) NO_PARENT=1; shift ;;
        --help|-h)   bash "$0" summon --help; exit 0 ;;
        *) echo "ERROR: unknown summon flag: $1" >&2; exit 2 ;;
      esac
    done
    if [ -z "$MSG" ]; then
      echo "ERROR: contract summon requires a <message> as positional arg" >&2
      echo "  See: contract summon --help" >&2
      exit 2
    fi
    # Auto-resolve parent from .drive_active sentinel if --parent not given
    # and --no-parent not requested. The drive sentinel names the organ
    # currently being converged; an Aiko summoned mid-drive is by intent
    # a child of that organ.
    if [ -z "$PARENT" ] && [ "$NO_PARENT" = "0" ] && [ -f "$HOME/.contracts/.drive_active" ]; then
      PARENT=$(cat "$HOME/.contracts/.drive_active" 2>/dev/null | tr -d ' \n')
    fi

    # Construct plan text. Aiko speaks first-person; reason is internal annotation.
    PLAN="$MSG"
    [ -n "$REASON" ] && PLAN="${PLAN}

(summon context: ${REASON})"

    # Resolve origin: walk parent chain to root via contract_core.get.
    # ORIGIN = the contract at the top of the lineage that contains this summon.
    ORIGIN=""
    if [ -n "$PARENT" ]; then
      ORIGIN=$(PARENT_ARG="$PARENT" python3 <<'PY' 2>/dev/null
import os, sys
sys.path.insert(0, os.path.expanduser('~/.claude/skills/contract/scripts/lib'))
from contract_core import get
